From: Lorenzo Battistela <lorenzobattistela@gmail.com>
Subject: Exclude constructors when resolving term variables
Upstream source: flip-engineer/bend fix-1236-ctor-shadow at da49ccd09f68cff69fefecd7a59aa2be94c897fd

This patch is adapted to Baton’s selected Bend source. The original change
added an optional constructor lookup argument to a newer resolver. The pinned
2.0.25 resolver has a simpler fallback, so this adaptation preserves its
existing return behavior except when an unqualified name collides only with a
constructor. The named-call parser also uses that lookup mode when it resolves
an unbound variable again.

This patch is for a future compiler-source release. It does not alter the
currently selected compiler archive or its lock.

